# UI/UX skill guidance

When editing Closar frontend surfaces, follow the project skills in `.cursor/skills/`:

1. **frontend-design** — distinctive visual direction; preserve the dark charcoal SaaS shell
2. **effective-ui-design** — WCAG 2.1 AA, 8pt spacing, fluid type, form/button hierarchy, reduced motion
3. **ui-design-brain** — component best practices and anti-patterns
4. **web-design-guidelines** — audit against Vercel Web Interface Guidelines when reviewing UI

Preserve the Closar brand:
- Wordmark **Closar**
- Tagline **Built to close.**
- Support **Generate leads. Close deals.**
- **Dark UI + light logo** (charcoal mark on light chip / light logo asset)
- Accent electric teal `#00E5C7`, warm amber for Sales sheet
- Syne + Space Grotesk

Prefer refining hierarchy, accessibility, and interaction quality over redesigning from scratch.
